[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Finding Fossil Man]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.46]Lesson 1 | 第1课
[00:02.59]Finding fossil man | 寻找化石人
[00:10.90]Why are legends handed down by storytellers useful? | 为什么讲故事人传下来的传说是有用的？
[00:17.43]We can read of things that happened 5, 000 years ago in the Near East, | 我们可以读到近东5000年前发生的事情，
[00:23.28]where people first learned to write. | 那里的人们最早学会了书写。
[00:26.92]But there are some parts of the world where even now people cannot write. | 但世界上有些地方，直到现在人们还不会书写。
[00:33.40]The only way that they can preserve their history is to recount it as sagas legends handed down from one generation of storytellers to another. | 他们保存历史的唯一办法，就是把它当作英雄传说来讲述，由讲故事的人一代代传下去。
[00:46.15]These legends are useful because they can tell us something about migrations of people who lived long ago, | 这些传说是有用的，因为它们能告诉我们一些远古人类迁徙的情况，
[00:54.22]but none could write down what they did. | 但当时没有人能把他们做过的事记录下来。
[00:57.67]Anthropologists wondered where the remote ancestors of the Polynesian peoples now living in the Pacific Islandscame from. | 人类学家一直想知道，如今生活在太平洋岛屿上的波利尼西亚人的远古祖先来自何方。
[01:06.91]The sagas of these people explain that some of them came from Indonesia about 2, 000 years ago. | 这些人的传说说明，他们中有一部分人是在大约2000年前从印度尼西亚来的。
[01:15.26]But the first people who were like ourselves lived so long ago that even their sagas, if they had any, are forgotten. | 但是，同我们相像的最早的人类生活的年代太久远了，就连他们自己的传说（如果有的话）也早已被遗忘。
[01:25.71]So archaeologists have neither history nor legends to help them to find out where the first 'modern men' came from. | 所以，考古学家既没有历史文献也没有传说来帮助他们弄清最早的“现代人”来自何方。
[01:34.84]Fortunately, however, ancient men made tools of stone, especially flint, | 然而，幸运的是，古人用石头制作工具，尤其是燧石，
[01:41.45]because this is easier to shape than other kinds. | 因为燧石比其他石头更容易打制成形。
[01:45.74]They may also have used wood and skins, but these have rotted away. | 他们可能也用过木头和兽皮，但这些早已腐烂殆尽。
[01:52.16]Stone does not decay, and so the tools of long ago have remained when even the bones of the men who made them have disappeared without trace. | 石头不会腐烂，所以远古的工具留存了下来，而就连制造这些工具的人的骨头也早已消失得无影无踪。
